{
  "dom_id": "step-e4650",
  "name": "Example: Identifying the Reflection of a Cosine Curve Over the Horizontal Axis",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/d7c097fe2f05014932d65b3599edb9d6976d493cc8560b77c8184d99d2395982.png)\n\nThe graph above represents a transformed cosine curve. What is the equation of the graph?",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/5ee965b666188ba4703400135c92c74e6188c8bc882855e84adb80a863d006f7.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\cos x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\cos x.$\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $6$ to give $y=-6\\cos x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-6\\cos x.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
